          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most repairs, DAP Plastic Wood-X is the filler to keep on the shelf: it stays put on corners, tells you when it is dry, and works inside and out. If you will be staining, start with Minwax Stainable Wood Filler or tint Goodfilla to match, and test on scrap. For fast painted trim work, FamoWood Latex and Gorilla are easy, inexpensive choices.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When the wood is rotted or broken, stop reaching for a latex tub. Abatron WoodEpox with its LiquidWood consolidant rebuilds sills and jambs that would otherwise be replaced, Minwax High Performance handles quick exterior repairs, and a J-B Weld KwikWood stick fixes stripped holes and chipped corners in an hour. Whatever you use, prime and paint exterior repairs, and caulk the joints instead of filling them.
